      ],
      "message": "fuzz: add end-to-end liveness target for parent and child relay\n\nCheck that if an honest peer announces the child of an acceptable\nparent and child, the child ends up in the mempool within a bounded\ntime, whatever other peers do. The target drives a real PeerManager\nwith real messages and validation, which the existing targets cannot,\nas they model validation results.\n\nAfter an adversarial prefix the honest peer only answers requests. With\nan outbound honest peer the adversaries keep acting; with an inbound\none they go quiet. Adversary connections are limited, and adversaries\ndo not refill outbound slots.\n\nKnown liveness holes are marked in the target and turn the check off\nonce opened.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-05T00:05:49Z"
      },
